<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62183" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέβης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>kettle, cauldron</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.362
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				1.26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίπους λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			; used for gifts and prizes, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.259
			</span></i>, al.; <i>brazier</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.100
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>coin stamped with a cauldron</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				4979
			</span></i>, al. (<span class="entity">Crete</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>, mostly the <i>basin</i> in which the purifying water
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χέρνιψ</span>) was handed to the guests
			before meals, made of silver, <i><span class="en">
				1.137
			</span></i>, al.; but in <i><span class="en">
				19.386
			</span></i>, a <i>pan</i> for washing the feet; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δολοφόνος λ.</span>, of the <i>bath</i> in which
			Agamemnon was slain, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1129
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			basin used as a <i>cymbal</i> or <i>drum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.58
			</span></i>; of the <i>gong</i> at Dodona, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				286
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>cinerary urn</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				444
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				686
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1401
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b> generally,
				<i>casket</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				556
			</span></i>: <i>pan</i> for colours, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
			</span></i><i>Bis Acc.</i><i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VI.</b>
			<i>vase</i> of cauldron shape on the roof of the temple of Zeus at
			Olympia, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				5.10.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>VII.</b>
			<i>air-vessel</i> used like a diving-bell, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				960b32
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
